Context: 6. Withdrawal of application for commutation on Medical Examination.

## 6. Withdrawal of application for commutation on Medical Examination.  
- (i) Permissible before medical examination;
- (ii) Permissible after medical examination, if pensioner declines to accept addition to actual age directed in the medical report, within 14 days of its receipt;
- (iii) Treated as withdrawn if pensioner fails to take the medical examination. - Rules 24 and 28.
